# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify redirect rules for the Pages deployment.
#
# /r/* share links — redirect to /?ref=:splat at the edge so cold visitors
# (no JS, no SPA loaded yet) land on the right page. The React route in App.jsx
# handles the same path client-side, but this catches the case where the SPA
# hasn't booted (first-paint, crawler, link previewer, JS-blocked browser).
#
# /.well-known/* is served as static files — no SPA rewrite, so apple-app-site-
# association and assetlinks.json are delivered with the correct Content-Type.
#
# Rules are processed top-down, first match wins. The SPA fallback MUST be last.

# /r/:code is handled by functions/r/[code].js, NOT here (#2214). Two attempts to
# express it as a rule in this file — `/r/:code  /?ref=:code` and `/r/*
# /?ref=:splat` — both shipped to production emitting the LITERAL placeholder
# (`/?ref=:code`, then `/?ref=:splat`), silently dropping every referral code.
# Cloudflare does not apply _redirects rules to a path served by a Pages Function,
# so re-adding a /r/ rule here would be dead weight at best. Do not restore it.

# SPA fallback — serve index.html for all unmatched routes.
# /.well-known files exist as static files in public/ and are served before this
# rule fires (Cloudflare Pages / Netlify serve static files first).
/*  /index.html  200
